**Link to the prototype: https://dumplinglover.itch.io/life-is-a-drag**

## [Life Is A Drag]

A visual novel prototype focused on a character named Jerome, who is on his first day at a college and meets his old classmate Shelly and a new classmate Marvin. This prototype integrates Yarn Spinner as a dialogue narrative system with Unity and is just a showcase, not an actual demo.

## Screenshots

![Room](Screenshots/room.png)
![Town](Screenshots/town.png)
![City](Screenshots/city.png)
![School](Screenshots/school.png)

## Systems I built for this prototype

- Uses Yarn Spinner's dialoguerunner as the main system for the game, builds a custom script to make it a singleton, and holds custom commands for yarn scripts.
- An IInteractable interface so the player knows that something can be interacted with:
  - Scene Loader: Scene transition when interacted with.
  - DialogueTrigger(Interactable): Play dialogue when interacted with.
  - Teleporter(base class implemented, to be integrated in the next chapter): Teleport and switch the camera to the destination when interacted with.
- Two dialogue trigger types: Interact and Auto.
- Crossfade system as a singleton which handles the fading effect (and also a loading screen in future implementation) on scene transitions.
- BlipPlayer implements IActionMarkupsHandler (Yarn's interface) to subscribe to the typewriter's ActionMarkupHandlers and plays a blip sound as each character appears.
- QTE Button/Timebar (base class implemented, to be integrated in the next chapter) that handles Quick-Time Events and sends a command to yarn scripts to start a QTE, waits until the event ends, and returns the result.

## Structure

- Assets/Scripts/: gameplay code
- Assets/Dialogues/: dialogue scripts
- Assets/Scenes/: scene files
- Assets/Fbx/: 3D assets
- Assets/Prefabs/: prefabs
- Assets/Audios/: audio files
- Assets/Fonts/: fonts
- Assets/Animation/: unity animation controllers
- Assets/AllSkyFree/: sky materials

## How to run

1. Clone the repo
2. Open in Unity 6000.3.8f1
3. Open `Assets/Scenes/Main Menu.unity`
4. Press Play

## Controls

- A/D: Moving left and right
- F: Interact with objects
- Space: Continue the dialogue
- Up/Down Arrow Keys: Navigate choices
- Enter: Select the choice

## Goals

Explore the area to find the next objectives, interact with the objects, read the dialogues, select choices and progress to the end of the chapter.


## Future Technical Improvements

- Animations for player and NPCs during dialogue
- More variety of animations for idling NPCs
- Cleaner 'BlipType' lookup
- Better dialogue UI
- Loading screen between scene transitions
- Integrate QTE mechanics to gameplay and UI (base class already exists)

## Future Story and Visual Improvements

The story and art will change a lot in a proper demo, however NPCs like Marvin and Shelly will keep similar personalities and designs. The demo will use a PC build instead of Web.

## What I have learned

This project was started as a research project and then later on developed into a playable prototype. This was my first time touching Yarn Spinner in Unity. There were only a few tutorials on YouTube, so I learned them through documentations and package sources. 

In the end, I managed to integrate Yarn to this project, learned about script execution order, singletons and shipped a WebGL build of this prototype.

